# Public site index and image tags (hard rule)

> **Every page and image published to https://analoginfo.com has one apex
> canonical, indexable HTML except /search, a non-empty alt on every img,
> and a complete ImageObject. Prove changed pages from a local copy
> first; one bounded live read of each changed production URL is the
> cap, not a full-site fetch. GPT 6 desktop follows the same steps in
> `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/website-and-ui/GPT6-INDEX-AND-IMAGE-TAGS-2026-10-10.md`.
> That file wins over the 2026-10-02 Astra note that said to leave
> production on noindex. Bandwidth, crawl, and image-weight rules in
> `public-site-bandwidth-budget.mdc`,
> `public-site-no-speculative-crawls.mdc`, and
> `public-site-image-weight.mdc` bind the same work.**

## Required on every content page

| Item | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Host | Canonical is `https://analoginfo.com` plus the path. `www` only redirects. |
| Canonical tag | Exactly one `<link rel="canonical">`. A script that reads `link[rel="canonical"]` is not a second tag. |
| Robots | No `noindex` except `/search`, which stays `noindex, follow`. |
| img alt | Never `alt=""`. The footer zoom dialog uses `alt="Enlarged product screenshot"`. |
| ImageObject | `license` = `https://analoginfo.com/terms`, `acquireLicensePage` = `https://analoginfo.com/contact`, `creator` = `{"@id":"https://analoginfo.com/#organization"}`, `copyrightNotice` and `creditText` name Analog Informatics Corporation. |
| Sitemap | `robots.txt` points at `https://analoginfo.com/sitemap.xml`. |

## Webflow

Head code and footer code each stay at or under 50,000 characters. If Save
stays disabled on "over character limit," shorten the new text. Do not drop
license, acquireLicensePage, or creator. Do not delete Google Tag Manager
or JSON-LD. Do not Prettify. Do not click Advanced settings Save. Publish
production `analoginfo.com` only.

## Proof before any "indexed" or "fixed" claim

Check the saved local HTML or a verified cache first. Then one bounded
GET of each **changed** production URL (named User-Agent, budgeted
client). One canonical, zero empty alts, content pages without
`noindex`, logo ImageObject fields present. Reuse the same browser tab
for layout. Do not recrawl the site. Do not fetch staging.

Use the Google live URL test and the Bing live URL test only for URLs
that actually changed and were not already accepted in this release.
A stored console snapshot is not the page. Do not repeat an accepted
live test to check status.

JSON-LD and Open Graph must also name the company and the two products
customers and partners look for. That bar is
`public-site-core-metadata.mdc`. Image license fields stay. Do not add
markup that does not name a product, a partner role, a contact, or a
required image-license field.

## IndexNow after publish

After a production publish of analoginfo.com, run
`docs/go-to-market/website-and-ui/scripts/submit-indexnow.py` from
pam-platform-docs with the **explicit changed indexable production
URLs** as arguments (at most 100). A no-argument run must refuse the
network. Do not submit the sitemap, `/search`, `/404`, or probe paths.
The script checks that `https://analoginfo.com/{key}.txt` stays on
that host and returns the UTF-8 key as `text/plain`, then POSTs only
those URLs to `https://api.indexnow.org/indexnow` as
`AnalogInformatics-IndexNow/2.0`. That root URL is the key location
for the whole host. It is a same-host redirect to the text file in
`/.well-known/`. Do not set the key location to the `/.well-known/`
address. That folder only covers URLs under it (HTTP 422 on the
homepage, measured 2026-10-10). Do not put the key in page copy. Do not
remove the key file or the root redirect. Google does not use IndexNow;
the sitemap and the Search Console live test cover Google.
